.TH "ORBIT" "1" "Aug 2026" "Orbit Developer Platform" "Orbit Platform Manual"

.SH NAME
orbit-port-list - List registered services (ports.yaml) or base ports for all projects


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBorbit port list [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
With a handbook/agents/workspace/ports.yaml registry, list every registered service by port with a live listener probe. Without one, list the 50-port project blocks. --limit and --page page projects, or services when a registry is found.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for list

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Print the result as a JSON envelope

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=0
	maximum projects (or services, with a registry) per page (0 = all)

.PP
\fB--page\fP=1
	page number to display

.PP
\fB--root\fP=""
	workspace root holding handbook/agents/workspace/ports.yaml (default: the workspace containing the current directory)

.PP
\fB--scan\fP[=false]
	Momentarily attempt loopback binds for every block slot (no effect with a registry, which always probes)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--config\fP=""
	Custom path to Orbit CLI configuration file


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBorbit-port(1)\fP
